  "instructions": [
    "1. Rinse the namul and pat dry with paper towels.",
    "2. In a large skillet or wok, heat 1 tablespoon of oil over medium-high heat.",
    "3. Add the garlic and cook for 1 minute until fragrant.",
    "4. Add the namul and cook for 2-3 minutes until wilted.",
    "5. In a small bowl, whisk together the gochujang, soy sauce, rice vinegar, sugar, and gochugaru.",
    "6. Pour the sauce over the namul and stir-fry for 1 minute.",
    "7. Add the green onion and toasted sesame seeds, and stir-fry for another minute.",
    "8. Season with salt to taste.",
    "9. Serve immediately and enjoy.",
    "10. Garnish with additional green onion and toasted sesame seeds if desired."
